# getppid-one-literal.baseline
#
# Known sites where getppid()==1 is still used as the orphan-detection
# idiom but have not yet been converted to the saved-ppid pattern.
#
# These sites are subreaper-unsafe (PR_SET_CHILD_SUBREAPER on any
# ancestor means orphans reparent to that pid, not init, so the == 1
# test silently becomes dead code).  They are pinned here only to allow
# the gate to pass while the per-file conversion work is queued.
#
# This list should SHRINK over time, never grow.  When a site is fixed
# (saved-ppid idiom added), remove its line from this file.  A new
# getppid()==1 literal that is not an orphan sentinel and genuinely
# needs to detect init as a process identity may be added here with a
# clear explanation; all other new occurrences must fail the gate.
#
# Format: `path/to/file.c:lineno  reason text`
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.

child/child-periodic.c:46  pending conversion to saved-ppid idiom
